        <h2 class="founder-name">Jon Ajinga</h2>
        <div class="founder-role">Owner, designer, and developer</div>
        <p>I started Pikes Peak Web Designs because small service businesses kept getting the same three lousy answers. "Put it on WordPress." "Pay us five grand up front." "Here's a template that looks like everyone else's." None of that fits a solo plumber, a three-truck HVAC outfit, or a family-run roofing company who needs the phone to ring next week.</p>
        <p>So I built something different. I design every site from a blank page. I custom-code it. I host it, I maintain it, and when you email me at 8pm because the contact form just sent you something weird, I am the one who replies. Not "the team." Not a chatbot. Me.</p>
        <p>That is also the whole pitch against AI page builders and Wix and Squarespace. They give you a site that looks fine in ten minutes; you have no idea what is under the hood, and when something breaks you are filing a support ticket with people who have never seen your business. With me you get the opposite: the person who wrote it, knows it, owns it, and can fix it in five minutes because they remember writing the line that broke.</p>
        <p>Your website is supposed to do a job: bring in calls, fill the schedule, answer the questions before someone calls. That is the work I am hired to do. Everything on this site (pricing, process, the toolkit, the changelog, the open Owner's Guide) is here so you know exactly what you are getting and why.</p>
